NAME
    cat - concatenate and print files or standard input

SYNOPSIS
    cat [path...]

DESCRIPTION
    Reads one or more files inside the shell sandbox and prints their
    contents concatenated in order, stripping trailing newlines at the
    end of the combined output.

    With no path arguments, cat passes piped standard input through
    unchanged. If no paths are given and no standard input is piped,
    cat fails with a usage message.

EXAMPLES
    cat /Logs/notes.txt
    watch log 1 | cat

EXIT STATUS
    0   All files or standard input printed.
    1   No paths and no piped stdin, path outside sandbox, file not
        found, or read error.

SEE ALSO
    head(1), tail(1), xxd(1), nano(1)
